            <ArticleTitle>Ovarian fibromatosis with minor sex cord elements.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>207-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ovarian fibromatosis is very rare, and the one with focal proliferations of sex cord type elements is extraordinarily rare. A 31-year-old patient developed the bilateral ovarian enlargements and complained of lower abdominal pain, Pathology indicated that these tumors were ovarian fibromatosis with minor sex cord elements. Our two-step operation involved the first right salpingo-oophorectomy for histological examination and the subsequent enucleation of the left ovarian tumor alone. The patient conceived 10 months after operation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
